# Python bytecode and virtualenvs — machine-local, and a .pyc committed against a
# different interpreter is worse than none.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# The model bundles ARE committed, deliberately: the service cannot start without
# them, and a coursework repo that needs an out-of-band 3MB download to run is a
# repo nobody can mark. If they later grow, or a training pipeline starts
# producing them, fetch them at deploy time instead and ignore them here.

# The DistilBERT weights behind the communication-collaboration model are ~270MB,
# past what a git remote will take, so this one bundle is the exception to the
# rule above. The service does not need it: without the weights it scores from
# the composite equation the corpus was labelled with and reports
# scorer=composite_rules. Regenerate with:
#   python -m training.create_communication_dataset
#   python -m training.train_communication_model
models/communication_model/
models/communication_model_checkpoints/
